; Regression guard: place-match index write on a str/txt is now a compile error.
;
; Before the fix (v0.4.31 and earlier): `no vet` was clean and the program
; printed 01 01 01 01 instead of 'bbbb' — the `str` RHS was bit-copied into
; a char slot, so the low byte of %str-long's length/tag field (1) was stored.
;
; After the fix (v0.4.37+): `no build` must fail with stridxwr (trace idxwrite)
; and name the allowed alternatives (push / push-str / fill / concatenation /
; []byte). `no vet` catches it too via the surface-AST place-match check.
;
; Trigger: `v str = 'b'` (a one-character STRING), then `s[i]: { ok -> it = v }`.
; The ok arm's `it` is the element place (type char for str, byte for []byte).
;
; Control: `v char = "b"` (char literal, double quotes) used to produce 'bbbb',
; but the language now forbids ALL index writes on str/txt regardless of RHS.
; Control: plain `s[0] = v` is rejected with trace `idxwrite`.
; Control: []byte / []i64 place-match writes remain legal.
probe = () {
    s = ' '.repeat(4)
    i <- [0..4): {
        v str = 'b'
        s[i]: {
            ok -> it = v
            -> _
        }
    }
    print(s)
}

probe()
